# ZGC tuning profile — RecSys backend service
#
# When to choose ZGC:
#   Sub-10 ms pause requirement (latency-critical inference path),
#   heap ≥ 2 GB, Java 21+ (Generational ZGC — ~50 % less CPU than classic ZGC).
#   Tradeoff: 10–20 % more CPU vs G1; not ideal for CPU-bound batch workloads.
#
# ZGC STW pause anatomy (all < 1 ms in practice):
#   Initial mark   — scan GC roots; STW ≈ 0.1 ms
#   Final mark     — rescan roots mutated during concurrent mark; STW ≈ 0.5 ms
#   Relocate start — select relocation set; STW ≈ 0.1 ms
#   All other work (mark, remap, relocate) runs fully concurrent.
#
# Usage:
#   java $(cat jvm-zgc.options) -jar recsys-api-*.jar    (Java 21+)

# ── 堆 (Heap) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ZGC needs 25–50 % headroom for concurrent relocation (copying while mutator
# runs). Rule: Xmx = peak live set × 2. Xms == Xmx avoids growth pauses.
#
# 2 g initial = warm start under load; 4 g max = room for traffic spikes.
# If allocationStalls > 0 in /health/gc, increase Xmx or add ConcGCThreads.
-Xms2g
-Xmx4g

# ── ZGC collector (Java 21 Generational ZGC) ──────────────────────────────────
-XX:+UseZGC
# Generational ZGC: separate young/old regions dramatically reduce heap scanned
# per cycle, cutting CPU overhead ~50 % vs classic ZGC. Requires Java 21+.
-XX:+ZGenerational

# ── 新生代 / 并发线程 (Young gen / concurrent threads) ─────────────────────────
# ZGC manages its own young-gen sizing internally; no G1NewSizePercent knobs.
# Tune concurrency instead:
#
# ConcGCThreads: concurrent GC worker count (default = ncpu / 4, min 1).
# Too few → allocationStalls under traffic bursts. Set to ncpu / 4, minimum 4.
# -XX:ConcGCThreads=4   # uncomment and match to your vCPU count

# Proactive cycle: trigger a new ZGC cycle every 5 s even at low heap pressure.
# Prevents old-gen spike when a traffic burst arrives on a nearly-full heap.
-XX:ZCollectionInterval=5

# Return uncommitted heap pages to OS after 5 min of disuse.
# Lowers RSS between traffic peaks without forcing an extra GC cycle.
-XX:ZUncommitDelay=300

# ── 栈 (Stack) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-Xss256k

# ── 元空间 (Metaspace) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-XX:MetaspaceSize=128m
-XX:MaxMetaspaceSize=256m

# ── GC logging ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# gc*       : all ZGC phases (concurrent mark, relocate, remap, STW pauses)
# safepoint : non-GC STW events (class redefinition, deoptimization)
-Xlog:gc*,safepoint=info:file=gc-zgc.log:time,uptime,level:filecount=5,filesize=20m

# ── Diagnostics ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-XX:+HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:HeapDumpPath=heap-dump-zgc.hprof
-XX:+PrintFlagsFinal
